The correctly rounded elementary-function module (elementary.wasm, RFC-0007), built by
`node scripts/build-elementary-wasm.mjs`, includes CORE-MATH binary64 functions from
https://gitlab.inria.fr/core-math/core-math at commit dae5dd8c0d5bd2691b45de28c9edbe12f067c3d3,
Copyright the CORE-MATH authors (Inria and contributors), MIT License. It also links soft-float
math and floating-point environment members of wasi-libc (wasi-sdk 29.0), derived from musl libc,
Copyright Rich Felker et al., MIT License, and LLVM compiler-rt builtins, Apache License 2.0 with
LLVM Exceptions. The module ships in the @nativr/nativr package as elementary.wasm; the upstream
license files are shipped beside it under licenses/ (core-math.LICENSE, wasi-libc.LICENSE,
wasi-libc.LICENSE-MIT, musl.COPYRIGHT). The CORE-MATH and musl license texts follow.

